# Cloudflare Pages redirects.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# Cloudflare Pages serves every page at BOTH /path/ and /path/index.html, and both
# return 200. Google crawled 17 duplicate /index.html URLs on this site, wasted the
# crawl budget of a brand-new domain, and surfaced /services/gutter-cleaning/index.html
# in search results instead of the clean URL. These rules 301 the duplicates away.
#
# NOTES
# - Placeholders (:name) match a single path segment and never cross a "/".
#   Site depth is 0, 1 and 2 segments, so the three rules below cover every page.
#   Do NOT swap these for a splat (*): a splat matches greedily across slashes and
#   only one is allowed per rule.
# - Order matters: the top-most matching rule wins. Static before dynamic.
# - Redirects are always followed even when the asset exists, which is the point here.
# - Verify after any change:
#     curl -sI https://www.progleam.co.uk/services/gutter-cleaning/index.html
#   must return 301 to /services/gutter-cleaning/

/index.html               /            301
/:a/index.html            /:a/         301
/:a/:b/index.html         /:a/:b/      301
